---
quiet: true
pre-compare: sort
---
// The DESIGN FORK PIN: the tetragon lanes' pre-INSERT records carry
// JSON-borne null-valued fields (the map's unmapped literal writes
// policy_name and the pod fields on every record; exec/exit records
// get policy_name: null), and Tenzir's serializer OMITS
// null-valued keys at write — irrecoverably, the row keeps no trace of
// them. Lab-verified 2026-11-05 (engine v6.20.1 → ClickHouse 26.10.3.7
// with the production DDL): a stamped record with
// unmapped = {pod: {name: null, namespace: null}, policy_name: null}
// stores an EMPTY unmapped column.
//
// This test runs the same stamp → round-trip → strip → verify chain as
// detection-verify-roundtrip and PINS the honest outcome: the
// null-carrying records (the exec/exit pair, whose stamped fingerprints
// cover the nulls) FAIL the recompute after the nulls are dropped —
// the strip cannot invert what the write destroyed — while the
// null-free kprobe records ride the same round trip CLEAN through the
// Process/File/Network strip arms. That split IS the fork: the
// recoverable mass verifies, the null-carrying rows keep flagging
// until the stamp side hashes a round-trip-stable canonical form (an
// operator decision — it re-specifies the fingerprint and orphans the
// already stamped rows; see the record_integrity README's round-trip
// section).
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_json
}
this = {tetragon: this}
homelab::tetragon::ocsf::map tetragon, ocsf
this = move ocsf
ocsf_derive
ocsf_cast
where class_uid in [ocsf_class_uid("Process Activity"), ocsf_class_uid("File System Activity"), ocsf_class_uid("Network Activity")]
if type_uid == 100701 {
  metadata.uid = "tet-attest-exec"
}
if type_uid == 100702 {
  metadata.uid = "tet-attest-exit"
}
if type_uid == 100700 {
  metadata.uid = "tet-attest-kprobe"
}
if type_uid == 100102 {
  metadata.uid = "tet-attest-file"
}
if type_uid == 400101 {
  metadata.uid = "tet-attest-net"
}
sort time, metadata.uid
homelab::record_integrity::attest authority_uid="tenzir-node-tetragon",
  chain_uid="tenzir-node-tetragon",
  genesis=false,
  chain="stream"

// ==== the ClickHouse round trip ====
// write side: Tenzir's serializer omits null-valued keys — THIS is the
// unfixable transform for the null-carrying records (policy_name and
// pod nulls on the exec/exit pair).
drop_null_fields
// write side: the absent typed-column fields lift as NULL — the
// tetragon maps write process.file.path (never process.path), the
// kprobe container block only when the process has a pod, and no lane
// ever wrote traffic.bytes (13,574,131 landed Network Activity rows
// carry zero traffic objects in the JSON, live count 2026-11-05).
if class_uid? == 1007 and process?.path? == null {
  process.path = null
}
if class_uid? == 1001 and actor?.process?.container?.name? == null {
  actor.process.container.name = null
}
if class_uid? == 4001 and traffic?.bytes? == null {
  traffic.bytes = null
}
// read side: the artifact strip inverts the injections above.
homelab::record_integrity::ocsf::strip
homelab::record_integrity::verify product="homelab-detection",
  title="Detection record chain break",
  uid_prefix="detection",
  scope_word="chain",
  windowed=true,
  link="stream"
// Pin the finding time for the baseline — the operator stamps now()
// live (the detection-verify-finding precedent).
time = 2026-10-10T05:10:00Z
